  ┌─ [1;35mquestion:[0m [35mFor the water access portion of the score, what condition qualifies as "water is available (either generally or at least in one room)" — should I count it as available when the water access status is 'Yes', or is there a broader set of statuses that also qualify?[0m
02:19:40 INFO   └─ [1;35muser answer:[0m [35mGood question! For water access, you should count it as available when the status indicates water is accessible in any form. This includes both the explicit "Yes" status as well as cases where water is "available at least in one room" — both of these conditions should qualify as having water access for the building facilities rating. The key is that we're looking for any evidence of water availability, whether it's throughout the property or limited to at least one room.[0m
