07:41:31 INFO   └─ [1;35muser answer:[0m [35mRecovery Value represents the monetary amount that can be recovered or salvaged from a returned item after it has been processed and assessed. In the context of return processing, it reflects the residual worth of the item—what the company can recoup through resale, refurbishment, or other recovery methods. This value is recorded in the financial management system as part of the cost breakdown analysis for each return case, capturing the economic benefit realized from handling that specific return. When calculating how much value we recover per day, we're essentially measuring the efficiency of our recovery efforts by dividing this recovery value by the number of days that have elapsed since the return was initiated.[0m
